WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.780
I want to take up in Volume 17, in July 25, 1924, and the heading says that the divine

2
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.000
will keep searching for souls who would lose all their rights, so that the divine will

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.880
might continue its divine act by placing all souls in their arms as it did with Jesus

4
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:33.840
on the cross. This is a very important section. So, Louisa says that this morning my sweet

5
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.760
Jesus made himself seen in my interior in the act of stretching his arms out in the

6
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:48.960
shape of a cross. "And I remain stretched with him," she said. "And then Jesus said

7
00:00:48.960 --> 00:01:00.400
my daughter, 'The last act of my life was to lay myself on the cross and to stay there

8
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:09.120
until I died.' With my arms opened, unable to move or to oppose what the executioners

9
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:19.040
were doing to me." I was the true portrait, the living image of one who lives not in the

10
00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:27.280
human will but in the divine. So, there goes all our romantic images of being flying high

11
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:35.160
and really having a good time that the true image of living in the divine will is the

12
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:46.520
crucified image of Jesus on the cross. Being unable to move or to oppose myself, having

13
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:52.720
lost every right over myself because it was taken from him, the horrible tension that

14
00:01:52.720 --> 00:02:02.200
was in my arms, how many things they said. And while I was losing my rights, others acquired

15
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:11.160
my life. Now that's the essential piece there that the person living in the divine will

16
00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:19.360
is living sacrificial love so that others may rise from the dead and live in God's presence.

17
00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:28.600
So Jesus said that as he was losing his rights over himself, others acquired his life. The

18
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:37.240
first right was that of the supreme will which using its immensity and all-seeingness gathered

19
00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:46.320
all souls, innocent and sinful, good and holy and placed them in my outstretched arm. So,

20
00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:53.600
here you've got the fulfillment of John chapter 10, 'I am the good shepherd and I lay down

21
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.920
my life from my sheep.' And then in the same chapter, Jesus says, 'The Father loves me

22
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.960
because I will lay down my life.' Now the Father loved Jesus infinitely, absolutely

23
00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:12.640
unconditionally, eternally, anyway. So that text is saying that the Father had a very special

24
00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:21.320
love for Jesus because he sacrificed himself to give life to us. So it's all about sacrificial

25
00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:32.840
love. And until we get the message that it is all about sacrificial love, it's all about

26
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:41.240
love, that is divine love, that's agape, and it's all about sacrificial love. That divine

27
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:50.080
love is sacrificial. It gives of itself to give life to others. So Jesus said that in

28
00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:58.000
his wide open arms, all souls, good and bad, were placed in his outstretched arms so that

29
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:04.280
he might bring them to heaven. So there you have this wonderful, wonderful image of Jesus

30
00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:11.480
as the great bridge, the Pontifex maximus, and he hanging over the abyss and the people

31
00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:19.080
of God walking triumphantly over his shoulders into heaven. Anything we achieve spiritually

32
00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:29.480
is through him, with him, and in him, we are nothing of ourselves. Jesus said, 'I refused

33
00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:37.920
no one, so this is love without borders.' I'm saying that slowly to make sure you hear

34
00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:44.080
it, love without borders. We don't ask whether the people believe or don't believe if they're

35
00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:49.040
in a good religion or a bad religion, if they're atheists or believers or whatever, we don't

36
