00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:14.760
and continue what my arms did outstretched on the cross. There you've got something

47
00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:22.320
absolutely divine, and that is that Jesus wants us to be a perfect replica of himself.

48
00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:28.560
And he is looking for those souls who will surrender all of their own rights, become

49
00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:37.640
a crucified love, small l, as he was the crucified love, all capital letters. And we

50
00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:49.520
become a tiny mirror image of him so that he can place all souls in our care as well.

51
00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:55.960
So he said the divine will wants to place all souls, the sinners and saints, innocent

52
00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:02.800
and wicked in the arms of the one who offers to lay herself in my will, in order to repeat

53
00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:10.300
and to continue what my arms did outstretched on the cross. This is why I have laid myself

54
00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:17.160
within you, Jesus said to Louisa, so that the Supreme will may continue its act of bringing

55
00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:30.000
everyone into my arms in you and through you. So now Jesus talks about what sanctity really

56
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.720
is.

57
00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:41.400
Sanctity he said is not formed by one single act. If you want to make a cardigan or a jumper,

58
00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:49.960
you cannot make it with one stitch. The one stitch has no likeness at all to the jumper.

59
00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:55.400
You need thousands of stitches put together in a particular pattern and in a particular

60
00:07:55.400 --> 00:08:03.360
way to get this beautiful garment. So the garment of sanctity is woven by many thousands

61
00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:10.220
and thousands and thousands of acts. Sanctity is not formed by one single act, but by many

62
00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:20.260
acts united together like putting your jumper together. One act by itself forms neither sanctity

63
00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:28.720
nor perversity because since the continuation of the acts is missing, the colors and the

64
00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:36.880
living shades of sanctity are missing. Do you remember that old saying that we got

65
00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:48.160
remember children? So an act, reap a habit, sow a habit, reap a character, sow a character,

66
00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:58.440
reap a destiny. But you must begin by sowing the acts. As I shared with somebody only today,

67
00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:05.200
if you sow one potato seed in your garden, you're not expecting a field of potatoes.

68
00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:12.340
Paul is quite clear about that in two Corinthians when he says that you reap what you sow and

69
00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:19.640
you also reap in the measure that you sow. So if there aren't continuous acts in the

70
00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:25.520
divine will, then the colors and the living shades of sanctity are missing. And because

71
00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:31.760
these are missing, one cannot attribute a just weight and value either to sanctity or

72
00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:41.040
to perversity. One bad act doesn't make an evil person. One good act doesn't make a saint.

73
00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:50.500
So, what makes sanctity shine and places the seal on it are the continuous good acts. These

74
00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:57.080
are the continuous acts in the divine will. No one can say he is rich because he possesses

75
00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:04.160
one coin. But those who possess extensive properties, villas, palaces, et cetera, et cetera and

76
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:11.600
a huge bank book, they can say they're rich. So it is for sanctity as well. And if sanctity

77
00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:20.520
needs many good acts, many sacrifices, much heroism, but can also be subject to gaps to

78
00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:28.640
intervals and so on, the sanctity in my will is not subject to intermittent phases. Once

79
00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:35.920
we get to the place of putting our will permanently in the divine will, that's it. We're clicked

80
00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:41.240
into the eternal will permanently. That's just the way it is. We're not going back to

81
00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:48.400
the human will. Up to that moment, we are simply going in and out of the divine will.

82
00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:55.560
But we have not reached this wonderful place where our will has finally and totally said

83
00:10:55.560 --> 00:11:04.840
fiyat miki sakondam verabam tuam. Be it done unto me according to your word. We've not

84
00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:12.440
really passed the test of being children of Mary yet. So Jesus said the sanctity of my

85
00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:19.240
will is not subject to intermittent phases, but must associate itself with the continuous

86
00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:28.440
act of the eternal volition, which never, never ceases, but is always acting, always

87
00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:37.440
operating, always triumphant, which always loves and never stops. Now here's a little

88
00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:44.520
bit of discernment for you that you can find out where you're at in the divine will because

89
00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:52.840
if your love stops or if you make an excuse that you know you don't have to love that

90
00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:58.720
particular person or love in that particular situation, these are the gaps which tell you

91
00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:06.400
that your will has not finally clicked into the divine will. So the sanctity in my will

92
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:13.880
brings into the soul the mark of the operating or the work of our creator. So the sanctity

93
00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:21.160
in the divine will actually portrays to other people, they can see it quite clearly, that

94
00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:25.960
this is the mark of the work of the creator. This isn't the work of a creature. And that

95
00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:35.280
is it's his continuous love. It's his continuous preservation of all things created by him.

96
00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:44.040
He never changes. He is immutable. This is what is declared in heaven in the book of Revelation

97
00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:53.160
chapter four and verse eight. The God who is who was and who is to come. The eternal one.

98
00:12:53.160 --> 00:13:02.560
The God who said, "Aego, Amy, I am." There was nothing else to say. That's it, complete.

99
00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:08.240
Who is subject to changing belongs to the earth. That's the low place, not to heaven.

100
00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:17.240
That's the high place. Changing is of the human will, not the divine. Interrupting good

101
00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:24.960
is of the creature, the low place, the human will. It's not of the creator. Therefore,

102
00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:31.440
all this would be on be fitting for the sanctity of living in my will because it contained because

